  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Homeland Security obligated $1.2B in federal contracts in FY2027 to date. The Department awarded 2,410 contracts, with an average award size of $493K. Obligations fell 98.4% year over year compared with the prior full fiscal year totals. Fiscal-year comparisons are uneven because FY2027 totals are partial (fiscal year to date). Past full-year obligations show material scale: FY22 was $20.8B, FY23 was $23.9B, FY24 was $23.6B, FY25 was $28.3B, and FY26 was $73.3B. Top categories for FY2027 to date include All Other Travel Arrangement and Reservation Services at $279M, Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $170M, and Security Guards and Patrol Services at $143M. Top vendors for FY2027 to date include CSI AVIATION, INC at $278M, GILBANE FEDERAL at $114M, and AKIMA INFRASTRUCTURE PROTECTION LLC at $69.6M. The figures above are contract obligations, and current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is ongoing.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What explains the drop in FY2027 obligations?",
        "body": "The Department of Homeland Security obligated $1.2B in FY2027 to date, down 98.4% year over year. The Department's FY26 obligations were $73.3B, which makes the FY2027 year-to-date total small in absolute terms. The FY2027 total is partial (fiscal year to date), which limits direct full-year comparison."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where is DHS spending concentrated so far in FY2027?",
        "body": "The Department of Homeland Security has concentrated FY2027 to date obligations in travel services and construction. The top NAICS categories are All Other Travel Arrangement and Reservation Services at $279M and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $170M. The top vendors are dominated by CSI AVIATION, INC at $278M and GILBANE FEDERAL at $114M."
      }
    ]
  },
